## Node name. Distribution listens on loopback only (below), so the node is
## reached from this host as {{name}}@localhost. For a cluster, switch to
## -name {{name}}@<host> and drop inet_dist_use_interface.
-sname {{name}}@localhost

-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## epmd, which maps node names to ports, still listens on all interfaces
## (0.0.0.0:4369). To keep it on loopback as well, set ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
## in the environment before the first node on the host starts epmd.

## Enable kernel poll and SMP
+K true
+A30

## Prod releases (rebar3 as prod release) use this file; development releases
## use dev_vm.args.src. RELEASE_COOKIE is required: it is the distribution
## cookie, the same secret on every node of a cluster, and bin/{{name}} refuses
## to start the node without it (rel/hooks/require_cookie). Keep this line
## last, so an empty value can never take the next argument as the cookie.
-setcookie ${RELEASE_COOKIE}
